WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.593 --> 00:00:04.781
Do you remember back in the day when...

00:00:04.863 --> 00:00:07.295
screen-to-body ratio was one of those,
like,

00:00:07.377 --> 00:00:10.266
headlining numbers in a new
smartphone presentation?

00:00:10.348 --> 00:00:12.495
Like, I remember, for a couple of years

00:00:12.697 --> 00:00:13.527
in a row,

00:00:13.741 --> 00:00:15.535
bezels were getting smaller and smaller.

00:00:15.617 --> 00:00:18.792
So those numbers got closer
and closer to that magical...

00:00:18.874 --> 00:00:19.704
100%.

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:21.453
And everybody generally
agreed that less bezels...

00:00:21.535 --> 00:00:22.365
equals better.

00:00:22.447 --> 00:00:25.111
The higher the screen-to-body number,
the better we were doing.

00:00:25.193 --> 00:00:26.023
It was improving.

00:00:26.651 --> 00:00:29.989
But then we started to come up against
the limits of display technology.

00:00:30.071 --> 00:00:33.151
So that's when we had to start
getting creative with things

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:34.759
like the Xiaomi Mi MIX phones.

00:00:34.841 --> 00:00:35.884
You remember those?..

00:00:35.966 --> 00:00:37.706
And then phones with curved edges,

00:00:37.788 --> 00:00:40.654
like Samsung started doing for
a couple years with that

00:00:40.736 --> 00:00:42.208
whole waterfall display thing

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:46.669
to make it feel like you had almost no
bezels at all on the sides of the phone...

00:00:46.751 --> 00:00:49.349
And we even got all the
way to that concept phone,

00:00:49.431 --> 00:00:50.635
the Xiaomi Mi MIX Alpha,

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:53.637
where the display curved all
the way around to the back.

00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:56.745
So they technically got to say
they- They had an over 100%

00:00:57.227 --> 00:00:58.270
screen-to-body ratio.

00:00:58.352 --> 00:01:00.039
It was a pretty interesting time.

00:01:00.121 --> 00:01:01.860
Now, we later,
of course, realized that,

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:04.228
you know,
we were getting a little bit carried away,

00:01:04.310 --> 00:01:06.050
and there are actually some downsides to

00:01:06.252 --> 00:01:07.809
curving the displays over the edges.

00:01:08.011 --> 00:01:08.841
Less durable,

00:01:09.055 --> 00:01:09.885
more reflections,

00:01:10.099 --> 00:01:11.489
accidental touches, all this stuff.

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:13.766
So, you know,
the curved edges started to go away.

00:01:13.848 --> 00:01:16.325
And these days,
we seem to have settled on, like,

00:01:16.407 --> 00:01:17.787
1- to 2-millimeter bezels...

00:01:17.869 --> 00:01:19.823
all the way around a smartphone screen.

00:01:19.905 --> 00:01:20.867
Like, that's just...

00:01:20.949 --> 00:01:23.269
That's just how premium phones...
all look now.

00:01:23.351 --> 00:01:27.603
It's gotten so good that some people will
actually see a phone that looks like this

00:01:28.165 --> 00:01:29.702
and leave a comment...
like this

00:01:30.504 --> 00:01:31.334
saying,

00:01:31.416 --> 00:01:33.189
the thickness of these
bezels is unacceptable.

00:01:33.271 --> 00:01:36.292
Which has always, to me,
felt a little bit ridiculous.

00:01:36.374 --> 00:01:38.532
Like, I see it as people complaining...

00:01:38.614 --> 00:01:41.922
about something that they were
never going to buy anyway...

00:01:42.004 --> 00:01:43.359
But fast-forward to 2026,

00:01:43.441 --> 00:01:46.174
and I get an email from
a company called Tecno...

00:01:46.256 --> 00:01:47.496
who wants to show their

00:01:47.698 --> 00:01:49.840
0-millimeter bezel to...
concept phone.

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:52.970
All right,

00:01:53.184 --> 00:01:55.837
I'll bite!
So I said, yes, it showed up...

00:01:55.919 --> 00:01:57.060
And here it is...

00:01:57.142 --> 00:01:58.715
This is a big...
premium

00:01:58.917 --> 00:02:01.714
smartphone with a 6.7-inch display...
and

00:02:02.436 --> 00:02:05.520
zero bezels, corner-to-corner,
edge-to-edge,

00:02:05.722 --> 00:02:07.120
nothing but display.

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:08.698
Well, actually.

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:11.304
Okay, hang on a second.
Is it truly...

00:02:11.304 --> 00:02:12.134
zero...
bezels?

00:02:12.216 --> 00:02:13.046
Like,

00:02:13.128 --> 00:02:15.255
I'm sure a lot of you are
looking at this and thinking,

00:02:15.987 --> 00:02:17.134
okay, if it was zero...

00:02:17.216 --> 00:02:18.095
truly zero bezels,

00:02:18.177 --> 00:02:21.352
wouldn't I just be holding
basically just a screen right now?

00:02:21.434 --> 00:02:23.850
I feel like you can see
some silver around it.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:24.989
How is it zero bezels?..

00:02:25.071 --> 00:02:27.030
And I know that you're thinking that,
because...

00:02:27.112 --> 00:02:29.709
that's what I was thinking when
I first took it out of the box.

00:02:29.791 --> 00:02:33.025
But what we're actually looking at here,
all the way around the screen

00:02:33.227 --> 00:02:34.756
is the literal frame of the phone.

00:02:34.838 --> 00:02:37.503
And we talk about the frames
on these phones all the time.

00:02:37.585 --> 00:02:38.593
This silver, the metal,

00:02:39.155 --> 00:02:42.430
this phone clearly does have a silver
mid-frame all the way around it.

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:44.529
But that is not the same thing...

00:02:44.611 --> 00:02:48.087
as the thin black bezel that
typically surrounds a display.

00:02:48.169 --> 00:02:50.077
So, like here's the Pixel 11 Pro.

00:02:50.279 --> 00:02:53.996
You can see the black is the
display's bezel and then the metal

00:02:54.198 --> 00:02:55.028
is the frame.

00:02:55.542 --> 00:02:56.485
So clearly, okay,

00:02:56.567 --> 00:03:01.369
now you can see that there's a difference
between a normal premium phone and this

00:03:01.571 --> 00:03:02.676
0-millimeter bezel.

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:03.905
Now, the secret,

00:03:03.987 --> 00:03:07.506
the way they're achieving this is
with internal display stacking.

00:03:07.588 --> 00:03:09.057
So it's a flat screen.
But...

00:03:09.057 --> 00:03:09.887
holding this,

00:03:09.969 --> 00:03:12.824
you'll actually notice the
frame is slightly higher up,

00:03:12.906 --> 00:03:16.339
slightly raised up from the
display itself all the way around.

00:03:16.421 --> 00:03:18.868
So you can feel the edge
of it with your finger.

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:22.588
And of course, straight on,
that means you don't see any bezel.

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:24.748
So you can say, yeah,
0-millimeter bezel,

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:26.961
but if you tilt it really far to an angle,

00:03:27.043 --> 00:03:30.017
or I imagine if you peeled
this frame off of this display,

00:03:30.099 --> 00:03:33.205
you'd see a tiny little bit of
bezel hidden underneath here.

00:03:33.287 --> 00:03:34.951
Unfortunately, this little edge

00:03:35.683 --> 00:03:38.585
kind of breaks the immersion of using...
a full-screen

00:03:38.787 --> 00:03:41.352
device more than any tiny
bezel probably would,

00:03:41.434 --> 00:03:43.379
just because now every time I swipe,

00:03:43.461 --> 00:03:46.195
especially from the top
to get to notifications...

00:03:46.277 --> 00:03:47.884
or from the bottom to go home,

00:03:48.446 --> 00:03:50.954
my finger drags along that edge.
So it looks...

00:03:51.036 --> 00:03:51.912
amazing, clearly.

00:03:51.994 --> 00:03:54.727
But I feel like actually using the phone,
weirdly,

00:03:54.809 --> 00:03:58.219
I'd prefer to have a little bit
of bezel and have smooth edges

00:03:58.421 --> 00:04:00.985
rather than having no bezel,
but having to feel

00:04:01.527 --> 00:04:03.529
the edge, this rough edge every time.

00:04:03.611 --> 00:04:07.770
And I think that answers the big question
of why this is a concept phone and not a

00:04:07.852 --> 00:04:09.735
real phone that they plan on shipping,

00:04:09.817 --> 00:04:11.701
because the rest of the specs...
are...

00:04:11.701 --> 00:04:13.045
solid.
It's a nice display.

00:04:13.127 --> 00:04:15.011
You know, it's nice and bright, 144Hz.

00:04:15.213 --> 00:04:16.890
There's triple cameras back there.

00:04:16.972 --> 00:04:19.306
It's a 6,000 milliamp-hour battery,
and it also,

00:04:19.388 --> 00:04:23.080
it's super lightweight to the point
where it almost feels like one of those

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:25.043
plastic dummy phones with no internals.

00:04:25.125 --> 00:04:26.100
It's kind of surreal.

00:04:26.182 --> 00:04:28.767
Surely all the YouTube
commenters hating on bezels...

00:04:28.849 --> 00:04:31.032
would love to try something like this,
right?

00:04:31.114 --> 00:04:31.944
I mean,

00:04:32.026 --> 00:04:34.706
they'd probably also still want
to see that hole-punch camera turn

00:04:34.788 --> 00:04:36.619
into an under-display selfie...
camera.

00:04:36.701 --> 00:04:37.825
But still, this is...
form

00:04:38.307 --> 00:04:39.137
over

00:04:39.351 --> 00:04:40.181
function...

00:04:40.263 --> 00:04:41.985
It turns out you actually
need a little bit of bezel,

00:04:42.067 --> 00:04:43.673
at least with today's display tech,

00:04:43.755 --> 00:04:46.712
to be able to have that smooth
experience using a phone and not

00:04:46.794 --> 00:04:48.200
drag your finger over an edge.

00:04:48.288 --> 00:04:52.353
And also to put a case on the
phone and not have the case...

00:04:52.435 --> 00:04:55.030
overlap onto the display...
itself.

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:57.014
This is more for Tecno

00:04:57.216 --> 00:04:59.943
to be able to say they
did something unique.

00:05:00.025 --> 00:05:00.855
I looked on

00:05:01.069 --> 00:05:02.936
the press release on their website

00:05:03.738 --> 00:05:04.568
and it says

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:05.990
this

00:05:06.204 --> 00:05:09.412
breakthrough on the Tecno next-gen
bezel-less concept phone...

00:05:09.494 --> 00:05:11.647
is much more than a design upgrade.

00:05:11.729 --> 00:05:16.180
It redefines how users will interact
with their phones in the AI era...

00:05:16.262 --> 00:05:19.436
by removing visual barriers
between digital content

00:05:19.998 --> 00:05:22.047
and the real world.
I

00:05:22.529 --> 00:05:25.134
would say relax,
they're hyping themselves up.

00:05:25.216 --> 00:05:27.004
I get it.
Surely this video is...

00:05:27.086 --> 00:05:28.289
feeding into that too.

00:05:28.931 --> 00:05:32.529
But you know what I didn't find
on that press release that they

00:05:32.611 --> 00:05:34.106
should be hyping up more...

00:05:34.188 --> 00:05:36.501
When I first took this out the case, I...

00:05:36.583 --> 00:05:40.005
unboxed it and I pulled it out
of this bubble wrap sleeve...

00:05:40.087 --> 00:05:43.335
and the first thing I noticed
was the back of this phone.

00:05:43.417 --> 00:05:45.209
And fun fact, the back of this phone,

00:05:45.291 --> 00:05:47.741
arguably more visually
interesting than the front.

00:05:48.303 --> 00:05:51.209
They didn't say much about it
in any of the press releases,

00:05:51.291 --> 00:05:53.387
but it's like this
holographic 3D butterfly

00:05:53.939 --> 00:05:54.860
wing type of thing.

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:56.933
It looks to my eye...
like it's...

00:05:56.933 --> 00:05:57.763
actually...

00:05:57.845 --> 00:06:00.521
coming off of the back of the phone,
like it's gonna...

00:06:00.603 --> 00:06:03.945
You're gonna have to take my word
for it because it's extremely

00:06:04.027 --> 00:06:05.739
difficult to capture on camera...

00:06:05.821 --> 00:06:06.935
But I swear this is...

00:06:07.017 --> 00:06:10.849
one of the best lenticular lens effects
I've ever seen with my own eyes.

00:06:11.331 --> 00:06:12.500
It's absolutely insane.

00:06:12.582 --> 00:06:14.900
So if they do ever ship a phone like this,

00:06:14.982 --> 00:06:18.271
they definitely need to make
a clear case for it because...

00:06:18.353 --> 00:06:19.183
it's crazy

00:06:19.654 --> 00:06:20.484
either way

00:06:20.698 --> 00:06:22.435
now, you know...
Thanks for watching...

00:06:22.517 --> 00:06:24.206
Catch you guys in the next one.

00:06:24.588 --> 00:06:25.418
Peace.

